[issue.1885]
number = 1885
title = "[Coherence] The checkpoint settlement document types are not deleted; only a three-line re-export alias is removed while the full types survive under layerx_types::historical::settlement"
revision = "3520b1428059af90261432778c008a9ce362a0b1"
verdict = "spec-edit"
evidence = "Commit 809b987fbc8561c22f2e758a552f78390df03aa0 deleted only the deprecated settlement alias, while services/agent/crates/layerx-types/src/historical/mod.rs:5 exports the declarations in services/agent/crates/layerx-types/src/historical/settlement.rs:8, services/agent/crates/layerx-types/tests/repair_22_33_1542.rs:255 and services/platform/hosted/paxeer/tests/repair_22_33_1324.rs:67 preserve archive parsing without current trust, and services/agent/crates/layerx-proof/tests/support/historical_checkpoint.rs:84 separately reads the document; therefore the done task at spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:279089 and requirement at spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:26843 must describe deprecated root-alias removal and retained historical readers, consistent with spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:192856 and decision 3022 at spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:11247, with the root-path retirement in spec/layerx-merge/interfaces.kvx:425070 and alias-only check at spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:279108 distinguished from deletion of historical declarations."
close_comment = "The deprecated layerx_types::settlement alias was removed, while the historical settlement types remain available for archive decoding without current finality authority. Task 9.26.3 and requirement 9311 should describe that alias removal and archive retention instead of claiming that all settlement document types were deleted."
